when war veteran frank castle returns  home from the horrors of battle all he  wants to do is be with his wife and kids  but after they're gunned down in a mob  shootout frank dedicates his life to  vengeance as the punisher a man with big  guns and an enviable 5 o'clock shadow  the punisher has been one of Marvel's  most compelling and complex characters  for decades for proof here are 10  Punisher facts you may not know the  exterminator the Punisher is best known  these days for his interactions with  daredevil but he began his comfo career  as a spider-man villain in the amazing  spider-man number 129 Punisher is hired  by The Jackal  to hunt for the notorious vigilante wall  crawler claiming that spider-man had  killed Norman Osborn in a previous fight  when in fact Osborn accidentally killed  himself creator Jerry Conway always  intended Frank Castle to first appear as  a villain only to eventually become a  hero well an extreme antihero obviously  the two made amends before Spidey got  completely punished the assassin Jerry  Conway Punishers creator originally  wanted to name the character the  assassin Stanley vetoed that idea  thinking it had too many harsh  connotations for what was essentially a  picture book for kids then Lee had an  idea years earlier he created an  unmemorable robot named The Punisher who  was one of Galactus his henchmen Lee  suggested that Conway used the robots  name  Conway took it because well you don't  say no to Stanley he's been the Punisher  ever since the executioner he starred in  over 600 books which have sold well over  200 million copies worldwide  except that we're not talking about the  Punisher these stats belong to Mac Bolin  a fictional character created by Don  Pendleton and if Mac Bolin didn't exist  Punisher might not have either created  in 1968 Mac Bolin is a Vietnam vet who  comes home from war only to watch his  family dive right before his eyes at the  hands of the Mafia which sparks a  lifelong obsession with vengeance  he earns the nickname the executioner  drives around on a weapons filled van  and keeps a war journal somehow Marvel  hasn't been sued into oblivion for  copyright infringement Archie and Eminem  get punished The Punisher is one of  those characters who's great on his own  but even better in a team-up like that  time he saved an  from an assassin hired by a group of  parents who hated his music published in  2009 in a two-part miniseries creatively  called  eminem / the punisher frank introduces  himself by killing Eminem's entourage  later eminem takes a chainsaw to the  villain barracuda and everything was  just as violent as you'd expect as  strange as it was all seemed natural  compared to 1994's archie meets the  punisher where our antihero chases a  drug dealer to squeaky-clean Riverdale  of course the drug dealer looks almost  exactly like archie so cue the comical  mix ups and mishaps the fun and games  end when the drug dealer kidnaps  Veronica but not to worry  Punisher saves the day and even sticks  around to chaperone the school dance  bombing the box office  Punisher has had three big screen  adaptations and two of them were massive  financial disasters 2008 s Punisher war  zone and the 1989 Dolph Lundgren  Punisher movie are the biggest bombs and  Marvel movie history how big you say  even bigger than Howard the Duck a movie  universally regarded as one of the worst  of all time no one laughs at a master of  quack fool yes even worse than that  dirty laundry Tom Jane turned down the  role of The Punisher a couple of times  because he didn't see himself as a hero  but after finally playing him in 2004 he  was hooked he walked away from the  proposed sequel due to creative  differences but he loved playing the  character so much that he starred in an  independent Punisher short film called  dirty laundry even washing black  t-shirts is a bloody adventure for the  Punisher Captain America's secret  admirer  Punisher doesn't really care about  anyone in the Marvel Universe with the  exception of Captain America cap was a  fellow soldier and the pureness of his  moral compass is unrivaled Punisher  actually respects cap so much that  Punisher has at times outright refused  to fight him when Captain America was  temporarily dead in the comics Punisher  changed his costume to a red white and  blue theme to honor his fallen hero  Frank Castle kills everything in a  one-shot alternate universe comic titled  Punisher kills the Marvel Universe The  Punisher did well just that in this  what-if type tale  Castle  wife and kids are killed during a fierce  superhero battle Punisher kills Cyclops  on the spot for his mistake which gets  Punisher locked away except on the way  to the prison he meets a group of others  who were disfigured during the Marvel  Universe's countless destructive  superhero fights  Frank Castle gets everything he needs to  kill every last character in the Marvel  Universe saving daredevil for last when  the deed is done  Punisher turns the gun on to himself but  it's not just superheros he's got it in  for in Punisher the end another  non-canon story Frank Castle is one of  the last remaining humans on earth after  a nuclear holocaust Frank tracks down  the last of the survivors to kill them  since they were the ones responsible for  the destruction of the human race again  Punisher kills everyone then chooses  himself as the final victim setting  himself on fire and wandering into the  wasteland finally ending humanity's  cycle of violence once and for all so  how does all of this add up well in 2011  Marvel Comics Editor Stephen whacker  crunched the numbers from 1974 to 2011  Punisher had killed exactly forty eight  thousand five hundred and two people  yeah he's kind of a monster in fact he's  literally a monster Punisher has been  killed and resurrected as monstrous  versions of his former self not once but  twice in the late 90s miniseries  Punisher purgatory Frank Castle kills  himself and that is brought back to life  as a demon hunter with two guns that  fire heavenly power or something like  that then in 2010 after being  dismembered by Wolverines son Punishers  body parts fall into the hands of the  vampire and Dave Navarro look-alike  Morbius who reassembles Frank Castle and  abused his corpse with life  turning him into Frank and Castle truly  one of the best comic book names ever  except for maybe Fin Fang Foom iconic  The Punisher skull logo means more to  people in real life than it does to him  hundreds of Iraqi soldiers wear the  Punisher signature skull somewhere on  their gear it's the symbol they've  chosen to represent their fight against  Isis  the trend has been going on for a while  but it was reinforced by Chris Kyle the  subject of the movie American sniper who  wore the symbol during his tour of duty  that cartoony elongated skull has become  a definitive rallying cry for  anti-terror forces in the Middle East  Frank Castle would be proud thanks for  watching subscribe  to our YouTube channel to watch more  videos like the one you just saw and  leave us a comment to let us know what  punisher facts you would have wanted to  see on the list
 

